#: ../../../../../../.conda/lib/python3.14/site-packages/pygmt/src/grdfilter.py:docstring
#: of pygmt.src.grdfilter.grdfilter:3
msgid ""
"Filter a grid file in the space (or time) domain using one of the selected "
"convolution or non-convolution isotropic or rectangular filters and compute "
"distances using Cartesian or Spherical geometries. The output grid file can "
"optionally be generated as a sub-region of the input (via ``region``) and/or "
"with new increment (via ``spacing``) or registration (via ``toggle``). In "
"this way, one may have \"extra space\" in the input data so that the edges "
"will not be used and the output can be within one half-width of the input "
"edges. If the filter is low-pass, then the output may be less frequently "
"sampled than the input."
msgstr ""

